<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela M-0 rises 0.7 percent in week to Oct 11.</title>
<headline>Venezuela M-0 rises 0.7 percent in week to Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's monetary base rose 0.7 percent, or eight billion bolivars, to 1.142 trillion bolivars in the week to October 11, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, base money stood at 873 billion bolivars.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 834405.</p>
</text>
